cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite this software and the associated BMC Ophthalmology article."
title: "Analysis code for residual astigmatism and toric intraocular lens correction in near-targeted cataract surgery"
version: 1.0.1
date-released: 2026-10-19
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Tabuchi
    given-names: Hitoshi
  - family-names: Shojo
    given-names: Tomohiro
  - family-names: Yamauchi
    given-names: Tomofusa
  - family-names: Gomi
    given-names: Fumi
repository-code: "https://github.com/HitoshiTabuchi/near-target-astigmatism-analysis"
abstract: >-
  Frozen release replay and independent reconstruction of the primary estimate
  for a single-centre retrospective cohort study of residual astigmatism and
  toric IOL correction in near-targeted cataract surgery. The principal
  estimates of the stratified, secondary and sensitivity analyses are archived
  as non-patient-level outputs and are not rerun by this code.
license: MIT
keywords:
  - cataract
  - toric intraocular lens
  - astigmatism
  - overlap weighting
  - multiple imputation
